<title>INDIA: India NSE puts circuit breaker on TELCO.</title>
<headline>India NSE puts circuit breaker on TELCO.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Stock Exchange on Friday put a circuit breaker on shares of truckmaker TELCO after the share slid 26.40 rupees or seven percent to 351.30 in late trade, brokers said.  </p>
<p>TELCO shares fell 27 rupees or 7.19 percent to 348.50 rupees on the Bombay bourse.</p>
<p>Traders said some foreign funds were sellers in the stock prompting punters to hammer the firm's share price on both exchanges.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
